bytes cat_num_divuit  0d 03 1b 05 03 1a         # divuit
bytes cat_num_dinou   0d 03 15 64 05            # dinou, o grave

# Twenty to twenty-nine. Catalan writes vint-i-un as one word with the i in
# it, and it goes in as one word here: the i cannot be a word of its own,
# because the conjunction i is a stressed content word in this module, which
# docs/status.md records, and a stressed i between vint and un is not a
# number anybody says. The unit carries the accent, so the stress goes to it:
# vintihú with the acute is [b i n t i u] with the u stressed, where without
# it the rule that reads the last letter put the stress on the ti. Twenty-one
# ends in the bare u, the way Catalan counts, and cat_num_vintiu below is
# the one the rule lays; vintiun is kept as the record of the other form.
# The paragraph above says why the h and the double s.
