# Three more tens. Each is exactly as wide as its insert now: the arm that
# lays down eight characters was given trenta and vuitanta a call each of
# their own, and noranta and setanta share one of seven. They used to be
# padded with spaces to the width of Castilian's word, and the padding was
# harmless while the halves of a compound were two words -- a space more
# between them changed nothing -- and is not now that they are one.
bytes cat_num_trenta   1a 18 02 15 1a 01            # trenta, for treinta
bytes cat_num_seixanta 19 02 03 1d 01 15 1a 01      # seixanta, for sesenta
bytes cat_num_setanta  19 02 1a 01 15 1a 01         # setanta, for setenta
bytes cat_num_vuitanta 1b 05 03 1a 01 15 1a 01      # vuitanta, for ochenta

# What goes between the pieces of a compound number: nothing. Castilian
# writes a two-digit number as three words, cuarenta y cinco, and
# convert_span_double lays down the space and the y with two calls; both call
# sites now lay down nothing, so quaranta-cinc goes in as the one word
# quarantacinc, and the accent the unit carries -- ssis, hun, dos -- is what
# puts the stress on it: seixantassis is [s @ S @ n t @ s i s].
#
# It was two words for a while, joined by the boundary mark and a space that
# IBM's own insert_space lays down, c7 then 48, because as one word the tens
# lose their vowel: the machine gives a word one stress and reduces every
# other a to the schwa, so the a of ranta goes where a Catalan speaker keeps
# it. Said as two words each half kept its vowel and its stress, and that is
# what was heard as two words, seixanta and then sis, and asked to be one.
# The schwa in the tens is the price of that, and it is the smaller fault.

# The d a letter rule lays in front of the voiced postalveolar to make the
# affricate of it. span_ph_Z_dur asks whether one stands before the Z, which
# is how it knows the fricative is the second half of an affricate and gives
# it the short duration.
bytes cat_ph_d 05

# The velar fricative's code, retaken. Catalan has no such sound: j and g
# before e and i are the voiced postalveolar here, so no Catalan spelling
# reaches phone 16 and the whole of the module's machinery for it -- an arm in
# the value chain, an arm in the durations, a record every neighbour reads --
# is standing idle. It is what a Catalan word-final r turns into so that the
# stress is placed as for a word ending in a consonant, and st_phnol.up's
# cat_drop_mute deletes it once that is done; ss_val.up says what one that
# somehow survived would sound like, which is nothing.
bytes cat_ph_mute 10

# The phone a Catalan word ends an n with. Castilian velarises a word-final n
# and Catalan does not, and the way that was stopped was to spell the final
# one with the interdental's code, which no Catalan spelling can reach and
# which the arm doing the velarising does not test for. st_strss.up is where
# the price of that is paid back: the stress rule asks whether a word ends in
# a nasal by the code as well, so it has to be told about this one too.
bytes cat_ph_final_n 0f

# The voiced postalveolar on its own, which is cat_ph_dzz without the stop in
# front of it. j and g before e and i lay one down or the other, and a rule of
# ours has to name both by address to choose between them: glob.up says which
# is said where.
bytes cat_ph_zz 12

# The glide and the fricative that ix says, as one insertion.
#
# Catalan writes the postalveolar after a vowel as ix, and the i is not only a
# graphic mark: caixa is [ka j S @] and calaix [k @ l a j S], with an audible
# glide that the spelling is there to record. Central Catalan is the dialect
# that drops it and Western and Valencian keep it, so both are Catalan; this
# is the one that can be heard, and hearing it is what tells calaix from a
# word that ends in a bare fricative.
#
# It is two phones from one letter, which is what insert_2pt_s's _4_2 form is
# for and what cat_ph_dzz above already does for the affricates. The glide
# first, then the fricative: y is 29 and S is 17.
bytes cat_ph_ysh 1d 11

# ---- the letters, as Catalan names them ---------------------------------
#
# A lone letter is spoken through span_char_name, the one dictionary of
# Castilian's that was kept, because a letter with no name has nothing to say
# and crashes. So x said ekis and h ache, which are Spanish's names for them
# and not Catalan's. A Catalan word cannot be put in that dictionary for the
# reason the digits found -- what delta-dict.py writes is named by an address
# the arena does not know -- so the way past it is the way the digits took:
# say them from a rule, out of bytes of ours.
#
# Six of the twenty-six are wrong to a Catalan ear, and the rest are Spanish
# spellings of what Catalan says anyway. be, ce, de, ge, jota and zeta are
# both languages'; efe and efa, ele and ela, eme and ema, ene and ena, erre
# and erra, ka and ca, ku and cu come out as the same phonemes here, since an
# unstressed a and an unstressed e are both the schwa. What is left is the
# six below.
#
# u_integ.up says where they are laid down and glob.up how. A name goes in as
# characters and the letter rules read it back, so hac is [a k] because h
# says nothing, and essa is voiceless because a double s is.
