# ---- the hundreds, the thousands and the millions --------------------------
#
# These go where Castilian's words stand, the way the tens do: each of the
# rules that says them pushes a symbol and inserts a fixed number of
# characters from it, so a Catalan word of the same width goes in by pointing
# the push at bytes of ours, and a word of another width by pointing the
# insert at the wrapper for that width. The hundreds are regular in Catalan
# where Castilian has quinientos, setecientos and novecientos, so the three
# arms that said those are not taken any more and every digit from two to
# nine goes the same way: the digit's word, then |cents and a space.
#
# Castilian lays down |cient and has the gender rules add os or as behind it
# later, once the gender is known, and insert_span_gender finds the word to
# add it to by its last four letters, ient. cents cannot be made that way,
# so the whole of it goes in at once and the two endings the gender rules
# would add are three spaces each. What is lost is dues-centes: a hundreds
# word is masculine here whatever follows it.
#
# c7 on its own is the mark IBM's data puts between the pieces of one word,
# quinient|os and nove|centésimo, and it does not end a word; c7 followed
# by a space does. So dos|cents is one word, and cent| followed by the space
# is a word with the rest of the number after it as another. Every string
# insert_l lays down starts with the mark, IBM's and ours: one that did not,
# nt after dosce, failed the insert and the rule backtracked into itself
# until the stack ran out.
bytes cat_num_cent_sp       48 0c 02 15 1a                          # " cent", where " cien" stood
bytes cat_num_cent_join     48 0c 02 15 1a c7 48                    # " cent| ", where " ciento" stood
bytes cat_num_centesim_sp   48 0c 02 15 1a 62 19 03 14 48           # " centèsim ", for " centésimo"
bytes cat_num_centesim_join c7 0c 02 15 1a 62 19 03 14 48           # "|centèsim ", for "|centésimo"
bytes cat_num_cents_join    c7 0c 6c 15 1a 19 48                    # "|cénts ", for "|cient"
bytes cat_num_blank3        48 48 48                                # where os and as went

